  "relevance_note": "Shows failure mode where startup routines encoded in project policy file are not reliably enforced because they are injected as plain text rather than executed steps.",
  "reason_included": "Concrete policy failure example (startup routine ignored) with explicit suggestion to treat startup rules as executable pre-steps rather than passive context.",
  "claim_snippets": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "claim_text": "Example startup routine in CLAUDE.md is expressed as an ordered list (read README.md and AGENTS.md, read relevant skills, check agent memory).",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "claim_text": "In the reproduced conversation, the reporter claims the model answered 'who are you?' with generic identity text rather than following the CLAUDE.md startup routine first.",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "claim_text": "The issue states that CLAUDE.md startup instructions are loaded into the model\u2019s context as text but are not executed as actual steps, so the model can ignore them (especially on simple prompts).",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    }
  ],
